      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Character Replacement Guide\n\nUse a character image for appearance and a source video for motion and scene structure. The H3 service must support Ref2VA and Character Swap LoRA loading.\n\n### Usage\n\n1. Select your character in **Load Image** and the motion clip in **Load Video**.\n2. In **Generate Video**, set `url` and `model` to your running H3 Ref2VA service. Keep `/v1` at the end of the URL.\n3. Fill the first **Remote LoRA** with the Character Swap file path on the service machine. Also fill the second Remote LoRA with the matching Ref2VA Turbo file; its strength is controlled automatically.\n4. Choose the **Turbo** toggle (strength 0/1; steps 50/8; video shift 12/6), check output size/FPS and the prompt, then run the graph. **Save Video** previews and saves the generated result.\n\n### Parameters\n\n| Node / parameter | What to fill |\n|---|---|\n| Load Image | Target character appearance. Connected as `image_1`, named `<Picture 1>` in the prompt. |\n| Load Video | Source motion video. Connected as `video_1`, named `<Video 1>` in the prompt. |\n| Generate Video / url | Reachable vLLM-Omni URL, e.g. `http://localhost:8000/v1`. Use the server address or a forwarded local port for a remote service. |\n| Generate Video / model | Served model name; normally `MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3`. Match the running service. |\n| Generate Video / prompt | Describe the replacement character using `<Picture 1>` and source motion using `<Video 1>`. The supplied prompt is a starting point; edit it to match your scene. |\n| First Remote LoRA / local_path | Server-local path to `h3_character_swap_v1.5.safetensors` or supported V1. This is not a path inside local ComfyUI unless both run on the same machine. |\n| Second Remote LoRA / local_path | Server-local path to `minimax_h3_ref2v_turbo_8step_v1.0_768p_bf16.safetensors`. Fill this path in both modes. Turbo OFF sets strength to 0, which the server skips. |\n| Remote LoRA / scale, int_id | Keep Swap `scale=1.0`; Turbo scale is linked to the switch (OFF=0, ON=1). Leave `int_id=0` for automatic identification. |\n| Turbo OFF | Character Swap only; uses editable **Normal steps** (default 50), video/audio shifts **12/3**. |\n| Turbo ON | Character Swap + Ref2VA Turbo; automatically selects **8 steps**, video/audio shifts **6/3**. The server needs room for both adapters and their composition; use `--lora-backend peft --max-cpu-loras 3`. |\n| Sampling / n, guidance_scale, true_cfg_scale | Keep `n=1`, `guidance_scale=1`, `true_cfg_scale=1`. Steps and video shift are controlled by the switch. |\n| Sampling / seed | Keep a fixed seed, e.g. `42`, when comparing settings. `control_after_generate=fixed` keeps it unchanged between runs. |\n| Generate Video / width, height, fps | Output canvas and frame rate. Template settings: **1344 x 768, 24 FPS**. |\n| Generate Video / duration | Set the complete target duration in seconds; the default reference is **24 seconds**. |\n| H3 Params / long_video, long_video_mode | Enable `long_video` for long clips. `full` generates the whole target together; `continuation` uses overlapping windows and requires backend support. For this workflow use `continuation`, enable reference slicing, and set window/overlap to **294/39 frames**. |\n| H3 Params / continuation_slice_reference_video | Enable synchronized reference-video and soundtrack slicing for each window. |\n| Save Video / filename_prefix | Output prefix under ComfyUI's output directory. The video is saved directly, including any H3 frame-alignment tail. |\n\n### Output\n\nThis is reference-guided generation. Other people, background details and action timing can change; this workflow has no subject mask. Output audio is generated, not an unchanged copy of the original soundtrack."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Character Replacement Guide\n\nUse a character image for appearance and a source video for motion and scene structure. The H3 service must support Ref2VA and Character Swap LoRA loading.\n\n### Usage\n\n1. Select your character in **Load Image** and the motion clip in **Load Video**.\n2. In **Generate Video**, set `url` and `model` to your running H3 Ref2VA service. Keep `/v1` at the end of the URL.\n3. Fill the first **Remote LoRA** with the Character Swap file path on the service machine. Also fill the second Remote LoRA with the matching Ref2VA Turbo file; its strength is controlled automatically.\n4. Choose the **Turbo** toggle (strength 0/1; steps 50/8; video shift 12/6), check output size/FPS and the prompt, then run the graph. **Save Video** previews and saves the generated result.\n\n### Parameters\n\n| Node / parameter | What to fill |\n|---|---|\n| Load Image | Target character appearance. Connected as `image_1`, named `<Picture 1>` in the prompt. |\n| Load Video | Source motion video. Connected as `video_1`, named `<Video 1>` in the prompt. |\n| Generate Video / url | Reachable vLLM-Omni URL, e.g. `http://localhost:8000/v1`. Use the server address or a forwarded local port for a remote service. |\n| Generate Video / model | Served model name; normally `MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3`. Match the running service. |\n| Generate Video / prompt | Describe the replacement character using `<Picture 1>` and source motion using `<Video 1>`. The supplied prompt is a starting point; edit it to match your scene. |\n| First Remote LoRA / local_path | Server-local path to `h3_character_swap_v1.5.safetensors` or supported V1. This is not a path inside local ComfyUI unless both run on the same machine. |\n| Second Remote LoRA / local_path | Server-local path to `minimax_h3_ref2v_turbo_8step_v1.0_768p_bf16.safetensors`. Fill this path in both modes. Turbo OFF sets strength to 0, which the server skips. |\n| Remote LoRA / scale, int_id | Keep Swap `scale=1.0`; Turbo scale is linked to the switch (OFF=0, ON=1). Leave `int_id=0` for automatic identification. |\n| Turbo OFF | Character Swap only; uses editable **Normal steps** (default 50), video/audio shifts **12/3**. |\n| Turbo ON | Character Swap + Ref2VA Turbo; automatically selects **8 steps**, video/audio shifts **6/3**. The server needs room for both adapters and their composition; use `--lora-backend peft --max-cpu-loras 3`. |\n| Sampling / n, guidance_scale, true_cfg_scale | Keep `n=1`, `guidance_scale=1`, `true_cfg_scale=1`. Steps and video shift are controlled by the switch. |\n| Sampling / seed | Keep a fixed seed, e.g. `42`, when comparing settings. `control_after_generate=fixed` keeps it unchanged between runs. |\n| Generate Video / width, height, fps | Output canvas and frame rate. Template settings: **1344 x 768, 24 FPS**. |\n| Generate Video / duration | Set the complete target duration in seconds; the default reference is **24 seconds**. |\n| H3 Params / long_video, long_video_mode | Enable `long_video` for long clips. `full` generates the whole target together; `continuation` uses overlapping windows and requires backend support. For this workflow use `continuation`, enable reference slicing, and set window/overlap to **294/39 frames**. |\n| H3 Params / continuation_slice_reference_video | Enable synchronized reference-video and soundtrack slicing for each window. |\n| Save Video / filename_prefix | Output prefix under ComfyUI's output directory. The video is saved directly, including any H3 frame-alignment tail. |\n\n### Output\n\nThis is reference-guided generation. Other people, background details and action timing can change; this workflow has no subject mask. Output audio is generated, not an unchanged copy of the original soundtrack."
